ga.text:
Selling, general and administrative expense increased by approximately $20.4 million, from $0.4 million for the three months ended August 31, 2025, to $20.7 million for the three months ended August 31, 2026. The increase was primarily due to the following changes:

• approximately $10.1 million increase in stock-based compensation due to the grant of restricted stock and restricted stock units to eligible employees and non-employee directors that occurred during the period;

• approximately $4.6 million increase in professional service expenses related to legal services primarily provided on discrete transactions and projects;

• approximately $2.8 million increase in personnel expenses due to an increase in our employee headcount during the period;

• approximately $2.4 million increase in lease and lease related expenses that were not directly attributable to generating revenue; and

• approximately $0.5 million increase in other general operating costs, including filing fees, insurance, and supplies, that were not directly attributable to generating revenue.

